Source: argus
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ronan Davalan <ronan@davalan.fr>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: argus
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gawk, gnuplot-nox
Suggests: fail2ban
Description: SSH attack counter and historical chart, no dependency required
 Argus counts SSH authentication attacks directly from auth.log — no
 Fail2Ban, no CrowdSec, no monitoring stack required — and keeps an
 unlimited-horizon daily history in plain text files, rendered as a chart.
 .
 If Fail2Ban is present, Argus also counts its bans per jail (reusing
 Fail2Ban's own decisions, never re-implementing detection) as additional
 series on the same chart. Never displays individual attacker IP addresses —
 only their daily count.
 .
 Installs under /opt/argus/, data under /srv/argus/ (world-readable, no
 sudo needed to retrieve a chart via scp/rsync), configuration under
 /etc/argus/. Two cron jobs: nightly collection, nightly chart render.
